</p>

<h2>What we build</h2>

<p><strong>Built-in shelving and cabinet walls.</strong> Open shelves, closed cabinets below and crown moulding across the top, finished to match the room. In a Kanata living room we built a full-wall unit with open shelving on both sides, an open centre above the cabinets and panelled lower doors. It ties in with the white mantel on the next wall.</p>

<p><strong>Window seats with storage.</strong> A window seat turns a deep window or alcove into seating and storage. In Barrhaven we built a window bench with three deep drawers and recessed panels that fits the alcove wall to wall.</p>

<p><strong>Closets and closet doors.</strong> Closet shelving, corner shelving with a built-in desk, and doors to close off storage. Options include bifold doors, sliding barn doors and double doors. In one basement we closed off a wide storage area with two pairs of six-panel bifolds.</p>

<p><strong>Custom bathroom vanities.</strong> Where a standard vanity won't fit, we build one in place. In a Barrhaven bathroom we replaced a pedestal sink with a stained wood vanity built into the alcove, with panelled doors, a white countertop and an undermount sink. When a vanity needs new plumbing connections, we arrange a qualified, certified plumber as part of the project.</p>

<p><strong>Under-stair storage, desks and nooks.</strong> Doors under the stairs, a desk in a corner, a media wall, or shelving in a basement family room.</p>

<p><strong>Cabinet doors.</strong> New doors on existing kitchen or storage cabinets. In a Nepean kitchen we built 16 flat-style cabinet doors in white with black bar pulls. See <a href="{{ url('/services/kitchen-remodel') }}">kitchen remodels</a>.</p>

<h2>Making awkward spaces useful</h2>

<p>The best built-ins usually go where nothing else fits: a sloped ceiling, a shallow alcove, a bulkhead, the triangle under a staircase. Because each piece is made to measure, we can work around baseboard heaters, vents and outlets, scribe the sides to walls that aren't straight, and run shelving right to the ceiling so there's no dust-collecting gap on top. The goal is a unit that looks like it was always part of the house.</p>

<h2>For homes and workplaces</h2>

<p>Built-ins aren't only for houses. We've built a custom office desk at a client's workplace, and we take on built-in storage, reception counters and shelving for offices, shops and condo units. Most of the carpentry and renovation work we do in homes, we can do in commercial spaces and condos as well.</p>

<h2>The design process</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Measure and talk.</strong> We visit, measure the space and ask how you'll use it: books, toys, linens, a TV, a desk. Photos of designs you like are a great starting point, and we can build from an inspiration picture.</li>
  <li><strong>Agree on the layout.</strong> You see the layout and dimensions before anything is cut, so there are no surprises.</li>
  <li><strong>Materials and finish.</strong> We'll walk through material, door style, hardware and finish options with you, and choose what suits the piece and your budget.</li>
  <li><strong>Build and install.</strong> We build and install the units, using a laser level so long runs stay straight from end to end. Then we add the trim that ties the unit into the wall and ceiling.</li>
  <li><strong>Finish.</strong> We'll agree on the finish as part of the quote.</li>
</ol>

<p>You get a written estimate in Canadian dollars before work starts, labour-only or with materials, and a schedule along with it. Workmanship is covered by our one-year limited <a href="{{ url('/warranty') }}">warranty</a>.</p>

<h2>Why hire a carpenter for built-ins</h2>

<p>At Zanini Renovations, the same company designs, builds and installs your built-in, so nothing gets lost between a designer, a shop and an installer. You deal directly with the owner, Jonas Zanini, from the estimate to the final walkthrough. Fully insured, with a certificate of insurance available on request.</p>

<h2>Where we build</h2>

<p>We build custom storage in Carleton Place, Beckwith and Franktown, Almonte and Mississippi Mills, Perth, Smiths Falls, Arnprior and Lanark County, and in Ottawa's Kanata, Stittsville, Barrhaven, Nepean, Riverside South, Manotick, Richmond and Carp. We work in Gatineau as well.</p>
